   This fails because after clicking the toggle on the only active item, it should be hidden (filtered to active shows only uncompleted items). But the step `I click the toggle checkbox on the todo titled "Buy bread"` clicks the toggle, which fires the toggle click handler, which now calls `updateFooter()` instead of `render()`. But `updateFooter()` doesn't filter the list - it just updates the footer. The list still shows the item because it's not re-rendered.

   The issue is that when a todo is toggled while on a filtered view, the item should be hidden from the list. But since we're no longer calling `render()` on toggle, the filtered list isn't updated.

   This is a real regression from my change. I need to handle the filtered view case. When on a filtered view, toggling a todo should either:
   a. Remove the item from the list (if it no longer matches the filter)
   b. Or re-render the list

   Actually, wait. Let me check if these failures existed before my change. Let me look at the scenario more carefully.

   The scenario "Active-filtered item hides when checked":
